WEBVTT

00:00:21.813 --> 00:00:23.019
Listen up, people.

00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:25.893
As long as nothing happens
for the next 15 minutes,

00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:27.849
our insurance
will be reinstated.

00:00:27.945 --> 00:00:30.937
So, let's just sit quietly
and run out the clock.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.616
A giant sausage!

00:00:39.248 --> 00:00:42.411
Oh, God, no! Get out of
here, you horrific sausage!

00:00:42.626 --> 00:00:44.617
Wait. Isn't today the parade?

00:00:44.795 --> 00:00:46.581
Lt's just a giant balloon!

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.120
Giant balloon?

00:00:57.307 --> 00:00:59.468
See, buddy, it's not so scary.

00:01:00.227 --> 00:01:01.342
I feel better now.

00:01:11.655 --> 00:01:14.067
Why are so many different
parades smooshed together?

00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:15.738
Lt's the Parade Day Parade.

00:01:15.826 --> 00:01:16.861
What's Parade Day?

00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:19.576
Lt used to be that
every group in New New York

00:01:19.663 --> 00:01:21.073
wanted their own parade.

00:01:21.456 --> 00:01:25.449
Why, when I was a boy,
we had a parade every day.

00:01:25.544 --> 00:01:27.751
Those were dark times.

00:01:27.838 --> 00:01:30.796
Now we just combine them all
into one big Parade Day Parade

00:01:30.882 --> 00:01:31.997
and get it over with.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.333
Hey, look,
a fog is rolling in.

00:01:34.595 --> 00:01:37.337
No, that's just
the Jamaican Pride float.

00:01:41.018 --> 00:01:42.724
Looks like
it's speeding up.

00:01:42.811 --> 00:01:46.144
Oh, no! Lt's within munching
distance of the Doritos float!

00:01:52.904 --> 00:01:54.690
Thank you.
Thank you.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:56.981
Kif, you're slacking
off on my waving arm.

00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:06.869
Oh, no. It's heading
right for those two nerds!

00:02:07.044 --> 00:02:09.000
Whoa.
Sweet shirt, dude.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:11.040
Thanks. I have
another one that says

00:02:11.173 --> 00:02:13.038
"Paleontologists
Do lt In The Dirt."

00:02:13.342 --> 00:02:14.707
I'm a paleontologist.

00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:18.544
I'll save one of you!

00:02:24.728 --> 00:02:28.095
Oh, honey,
I dig you so much.

00:02:28.523 --> 00:02:31.640
Thank you for saving
my stupidly-dressed husband.

00:02:31.735 --> 00:02:33.225
You're a hero.

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:37.020
A hero, indeed.
What's your name, son?

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:38.321
I don't know. Fry?

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:40.490
Ladies and gentlemen,
I'm proud

00:02:40.577 --> 00:02:42.909
to associate myself with a true hero.

00:02:45.582 --> 00:02:49.825
Mr. Fry, allow me to present
you with the keys to the city!

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.003
This one's for the deadbolt,
this is for the top lock.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.626
I think this
one's for the knob.

00:02:54.758 --> 00:02:56.339
The city's in
a bad neighborhood.

00:02:56.426 --> 00:02:57.711
Care to say a few words, son?

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.129
Uh...

00:02:59.221 --> 00:03:02.554
Heroes don't do drugs.
Except for Drugman, I guess.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:07.596
I hereby declare
that henceforth,

00:03:07.688 --> 00:03:11.351
this Saturday shall
be known as Fry-Day!

00:03:20.409 --> 00:03:23.993
Lt sure was nice of the mayor's
wife to have sex with me. Uh?

00:03:24.621 --> 00:03:26.532
You.
What?

00:03:26.707 --> 00:03:29.995
You could have saved a robot,
but instead, you saved a human.

00:03:30.085 --> 00:03:33.202
Do you think human life is
more precious than robot life?

00:03:33.296 --> 00:03:34.786
No, no.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.455
Well, yes, actually.

00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:39.249
That's it.
I'm killing myself.

00:03:39.386 --> 00:03:40.375
Oh, lord.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:43.803
Don't try to talk
me out of it! Well?

00:03:44.015 --> 00:03:46.597
Bender, you always say
you're going to kill yourself,

00:03:46.685 --> 00:03:47.891
but you almost never do.

00:03:48.186 --> 00:03:50.643
Yeah. Last time you went
to the suicide booth,

00:03:50.731 --> 00:03:52.517
you ended up dating
it for six months.

00:03:52.858 --> 00:03:54.348
How is Lynn, by the way?

00:03:54.526 --> 00:03:56.812
Living in Oregon
with her crazy mother.

00:03:57.195 --> 00:03:59.686
See you at my funeral,
suckers!

00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:07.069
Kill me, please,
and make it splatter!

00:04:07.164 --> 00:04:09.997
With pleasure, Bender.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.449
Lynn? Huh. Wow,
you look great.

00:04:13.295 --> 00:04:15.661
Fat, but great.
I thought you were in Oregon.

00:04:15.839 --> 00:04:19.582
My mom tried to commit suicide in
me. I don't want to talk about it.

00:04:19.676 --> 00:04:21.587
Well, tell your mom
I said "hello,"

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.585
and it's been nice
catching up with you.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.261
Let's get this
show on the road.

00:04:25.348 --> 00:04:29.842
Oh, no. You're going to die, all
right, but it won't be suicide.

00:04:29.978 --> 00:04:31.843
It'II be murder.

00:04:41.031 --> 00:04:42.271
Missed me!

00:04:54.461 --> 00:04:57.544
He did it!
He actually did it this time.

00:04:59.591 --> 00:05:01.798
No way, mon.
He's faking it.

00:05:04.429 --> 00:05:08.297
He really is gone! Everyone,
put on your taking-off caps.

00:05:08.892 --> 00:05:09.972
Our what?

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:12.176
Lt's a sign of respect,
you savage!

00:05:15.774 --> 00:05:18.561
Poor, nasty,
mean old Bender.

00:05:18.944 --> 00:05:21.856
I can't believe we'll never
hear his evil laugh again.

00:05:35.919 --> 00:05:37.284
I miss him so much.

00:05:37.587 --> 00:05:38.997
There, there, Fry.

00:05:39.089 --> 00:05:43.503
He may be gone, but he'll
always be with us as a trash can.

00:05:46.763 --> 00:05:49.254
Look at that loser getting
garbage dumped in him.

00:05:49.391 --> 00:05:51.006
Glad I'm not him,
whoever he is.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:55.473
Fry, as his only friend, you should
have first pick of body parts.

00:05:55.564 --> 00:05:58.931
Just don't pick his nose!
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

00:05:59.276 --> 00:06:01.688
What's wrong with you guys?
This is comedy gold.

00:06:01.945 --> 00:06:04.732
He always had my back.
So I'll take his arm.

00:06:04.823 --> 00:06:06.609
As a back-scratcher.

00:06:09.744 --> 00:06:10.779
I love you, Bender!

00:06:11.246 --> 00:06:12.907
Somebody hand
me a bolt cutter.

00:06:12.998 --> 00:06:16.707
Hey, dip-schlitz, that's not
me. I'm right here. Hello?

00:06:18.712 --> 00:06:20.498
Pay attention to me!

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:24.501
Why can't anybody
hear my witty remarks?

00:06:24.593 --> 00:06:26.174
This is hell.

00:06:26.261 --> 00:06:27.250
You wish.

00:06:28.471 --> 00:06:30.757
Robot devil?
You can hear me?

00:06:30.849 --> 00:06:32.385
Why is everyone
else ignoring me?

00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:34.466
Isn't it obvious, Bender?

00:06:34.561 --> 00:06:35.676
Yeah, I guess it is.

00:06:35.854 --> 00:06:37.139
You're dead!

00:06:37.314 --> 00:06:40.898
What? I thought I just had
laryngitis and antigravity.

00:06:40.984 --> 00:06:45.102
Come down to my office
and I'll explain everything.

00:06:51.703 --> 00:06:52.863
So what's
happening to me?

00:06:53.121 --> 00:06:55.658
And I'll take my answer
in any form but a song.

00:06:55.832 --> 00:06:57.572
Oh, you're no fun.

00:06:59.044 --> 00:07:02.411
You see, Bender, it's
simple. You're a ghost.

00:07:02.672 --> 00:07:04.208
A ghost?

00:07:04.341 --> 00:07:06.332
No, just the regular kind.

00:07:07.344 --> 00:07:10.131
Because you killed yourself,
you're in limbo.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:13.843
Your software was exported
to the computational cloud.

00:07:14.059 --> 00:07:16.596
Adoy. Wait. Adoy?

00:07:16.811 --> 00:07:18.426
Your disembodied
program is now

00:07:18.563 --> 00:07:20.178
running on the
wireless network

00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:21.888
shared by all machinery.

00:07:21.983 --> 00:07:23.348
Cut to the chase,
smokey.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:24.941
How do I get out of limbo?

00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:28.402
That's the laughy part.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:31.482
You can't! You're stuck
in an infinite loop.

00:07:32.869 --> 00:07:35.531
An infinite loop?
I don't have time for that!

00:07:35.622 --> 00:07:37.362
Man, this is
all Fry's fault.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:41.283
Fry? I hate that guy.
We once traded hands.

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:44.456
They still stink
of candy corn.

00:07:44.631 --> 00:07:46.587
Get this. That jerk
said human life

00:07:46.716 --> 00:07:48.707
was more valuable
than robot life.

00:07:49.052 --> 00:07:52.215
What? After all
you've done for him?

00:07:52.305 --> 00:07:53.795
Fry must die!

00:07:54.057 --> 00:07:57.720
I know, right? I'd murder him
good, if only I was still alive.

00:07:58.019 --> 00:07:59.008
Hmm...

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:02.182
Bender, would you
like to make a deal?

00:08:02.273 --> 00:08:03.683
I'm not stupid.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.561
So, yes, absolutely.

00:08:06.695 --> 00:08:07.980
What have I agreed to?

00:08:08.071 --> 00:08:10.278
I'll return you
to your body

00:08:10.365 --> 00:08:16.076
after you use your ghostly
powers to scare Fry to death.

00:08:18.748 --> 00:08:20.534
That sounds fair
and also fun.

00:08:20.625 --> 00:08:22.456
I like that there's
no catch this time.

00:08:22.544 --> 00:08:24.080
But, wait.
There's a catch.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.285
Crap!

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:30.044
Lf you fail, you'll spend
eternity here in robot hell.

00:08:30.218 --> 00:08:33.051
Which, as luck would have it,
is where I rehearse my band.

00:08:33.138 --> 00:08:34.218
Hit it, boys!

00:08:36.349 --> 00:08:38.635
Cigars are evil,
you won't miss 'em...

00:08:38.727 --> 00:08:42.515
Okay, I'll do it, I'll do it!
Just stop the damn music!

00:08:47.986 --> 00:08:51.069
Scare Fry to death? Ha!
I could do that in my sleep.

00:08:51.614 --> 00:08:53.980
Whoo! Whoo-oo-oo-oo!

00:08:54.451 --> 00:08:55.782
What are you? Deaf?

00:08:55.952 --> 00:08:57.943
Whoo! Whoo!

00:09:14.345 --> 00:09:17.178
Hmm. Soap. I know
Fry's afraid of that.

00:09:17.557 --> 00:09:21.175
Maybe he'll die if I rub him
all over with it, real slow.

00:09:27.776 --> 00:09:30.813
Whoa, sick! My software
can control electronics!

00:09:32.322 --> 00:09:33.311
What the...

00:09:39.204 --> 00:09:42.071
No! Not the armpits!
Winter's coming!

00:09:44.167 --> 00:09:46.374
As you can see,
since Bender's death,

00:09:46.461 --> 00:09:50.579
requests to bite one's
shiny metal ass are down 98%.

00:09:53.218 --> 00:09:54.674
Do you mind
doing that later?

00:09:54.761 --> 00:09:56.717
Bite my shiny metal ass.

00:09:57.305 --> 00:09:59.546
Help! I was attacked
in my bathroom!

00:09:59.641 --> 00:10:02.223
By my bathroom!
I'm being haunted by a ghost!

00:10:05.355 --> 00:10:08.847
Fry, you're just upset because
you drove Bender to suicide.

00:10:08.942 --> 00:10:12.651
Here. Take your mind off it with
these soothing relaxation balls.

00:10:14.531 --> 00:10:18.570
All right. I got him all heebie-jeebied
with my bathroom of horrors.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:21.026
One more good scare,
and I'll be out of limbo.

00:10:21.329 --> 00:10:23.365
Ooh. Did someone say limbo?

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:25.280
No.
Nothing.

00:10:25.583 --> 00:10:28.791
Hold onto your dookie.
It's about to get spooky!

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:59.527
I'm telling you, something
supernatural is happening.

00:10:59.617 --> 00:11:00.823
I'm scared to death!

00:11:02.787 --> 00:11:04.027
Stop being ridiculous.

00:11:04.122 --> 00:11:06.238
There's no such thing
as whatever you're saying.

00:11:07.542 --> 00:11:08.531
Ow, ow, ow!

00:11:09.043 --> 00:11:12.581
Whoa, maybe you're right. I
only meant to slap you twice.

00:11:12.839 --> 00:11:16.002
All I know is I've got a
ghost that needs busting.

00:11:16.092 --> 00:11:17.081
Who you gonna call?

00:11:17.218 --> 00:11:18.253
Gho...

00:11:18.344 --> 00:11:22.337
The number you have dialed
has been lame since 1989.

00:11:26.227 --> 00:11:27.262
Now do you believe me?

00:11:27.437 --> 00:11:31.180
Oh, Fuff, enough of
your superstitious nonsense.

00:11:31.274 --> 00:11:35.438
I'm sure that whatever is happening
can be explained by science.

00:11:36.237 --> 00:11:38.353
Let the seance begin.

00:11:38.448 --> 00:11:39.904
I said science!

00:11:48.124 --> 00:11:49.785
The veil is lifting.

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:54.874
I am gazing into the
spirit world, and nothing.

00:11:55.173 --> 00:11:56.583
You said something
about a buffet?

00:11:56.966 --> 00:11:58.752
I'm right here,
you lazy shyster.

00:12:03.139 --> 00:12:05.255
Wait, I'm sensing something.

00:12:07.227 --> 00:12:09.058
I'm rich.

00:12:09.354 --> 00:12:10.343
Ow!

00:12:10.521 --> 00:12:11.556
Is it a ghost?

00:12:11.648 --> 00:12:14.606
There's no such thing as
ghosts, you donkey-monkey.

00:12:14.692 --> 00:12:16.102
It's a robot ghost.

00:12:17.654 --> 00:12:18.939
A robot ghost?

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:21.021
What robot would
want to haunt me?

00:12:21.115 --> 00:12:24.278
Me, dumbass. Bender,
Bender, Bender, Bender!

00:12:24.535 --> 00:12:27.151
Ah, tell him,
you baggy old crone.

00:12:34.337 --> 00:12:37.329
Finally. Any more
ridiculous ideas?

00:12:38.716 --> 00:12:40.456
Hallelujah.

00:12:44.305 --> 00:12:46.341
I'm here to
conduct the exorcism

00:12:46.474 --> 00:12:48.510
and avail myself
of the buffet.

00:12:48.893 --> 00:12:51.100
Can I get an amen
and a goodly helping

00:12:51.229 --> 00:12:53.436
of Scruffy's
famous corn biscuits?

00:12:53.523 --> 00:12:54.512
Right away, Reverend.

00:12:56.234 --> 00:13:00.273
Oh, lord. I got
the too-much-macaroni sweats.

00:13:00.363 --> 00:13:02.604
Now, where is this
alleged apparition?

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.736
Might be a problem with your
circuit breaker. See you.

00:13:09.831 --> 00:13:12.493
Please, I'm under
constant attack by machinery.

00:13:12.667 --> 00:13:15.750
I can't sleep, I can't think,
I can't even think.

00:13:17.088 --> 00:13:18.168
Very well.

00:13:20.008 --> 00:13:22.875
This sacramental
firewall scans for

00:13:22.969 --> 00:13:25.551
and removes ghostware
in a 20 foot radius.

00:13:25.888 --> 00:13:27.219
Bring it on, holy man.

00:13:33.062 --> 00:13:36.520
Carry this at all times
and the demon cannot harm you.

00:13:36.899 --> 00:13:39.732
It also keeps cats off
the sofa by killing 'em.

00:13:58.629 --> 00:14:02.963
Ah. So quiet, so peaceful.

00:14:03.426 --> 00:14:05.382
Time to lower my guard
even for a minute.

00:14:10.767 --> 00:14:11.722
Ow!

00:14:13.227 --> 00:14:14.763
Heart attack.

00:14:15.438 --> 00:14:16.848
Yep, I was right.

00:14:24.113 --> 00:14:26.024
Okay, Beelzy,
Fry's dead.

00:14:26.115 --> 00:14:27.446
A ghost!

00:14:27.575 --> 00:14:28.655
Oh, it's you.

00:14:28.743 --> 00:14:30.734
A deal's a deal, so
give me my body back.

00:14:31.245 --> 00:14:33.236
Fry's dead, you say?

00:14:33.539 --> 00:14:37.248
Funny, that's not what it says
on his Wikipedia page.

00:14:38.419 --> 00:14:40.455
Survived a heart attack?

00:14:40.797 --> 00:14:42.958
Damn you, Obama-care!

00:14:45.301 --> 00:14:48.418
I'm afraid your heart has
suffered a lot of damage, Mr. Fry,

00:14:48.513 --> 00:14:50.128
and my cleavage
isn't helping.

00:14:50.264 --> 00:14:51.845
Not helping him.

00:14:52.225 --> 00:14:54.307
One more sudden shock will kill you.

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:58.553
Sudden? That's just the kind of
one more shock I was planning.

00:15:01.818 --> 00:15:03.934
The machines,
they're after me.

00:15:04.028 --> 00:15:06.360
You're suffering
from machine phobia.

00:15:06.447 --> 00:15:08.984
Your only hope is to go
to the Amish Home World,

00:15:09.075 --> 00:15:10.440
where no machines are allowed.

00:15:10.993 --> 00:15:13.575
I guess
it's for the best.

00:15:13.663 --> 00:15:14.823
Whoo...

00:15:14.914 --> 00:15:18.156
The only machine I'll
ever miss is Bender.

00:15:18.334 --> 00:15:19.574
Say what?

00:15:19.669 --> 00:15:24.083
Now that he's gone, I realize
how valuable a robot life can be,

00:15:24.173 --> 00:15:26.209
when it belongs
to my best friend.

00:15:27.969 --> 00:15:30.460
That's the closest
thing to "Bender is great"

00:15:30.555 --> 00:15:33.843
that anyone besides me
has ever said.

00:15:35.351 --> 00:15:39.185
Final boarding call for Flight
38 to the Amish Home World.

00:15:39.272 --> 00:15:44.016
As a reminder, passengers are
limited to two carry-on butter churns.

00:15:45.778 --> 00:15:49.316
I'm sorry, Fry, I'm sorry.
Wait for your ghost-buddy.

00:16:53.104 --> 00:16:55.060
Brother Fry,
thou hast visltors.

00:16:55.690 --> 00:16:57.351
Hi, Fry. Hello.
Hey, how have you been?

00:16:57.608 --> 00:17:00.975
Well, yank my beard.
This be a surprise.

00:17:02.530 --> 00:17:03.610
How are you, Fry?

00:17:03.781 --> 00:17:05.191
Thank you for asking, English.

00:17:05.283 --> 00:17:08.525
My life is simple but plain,
and though Bender be gone,

00:17:08.619 --> 00:17:11.531
somehow I feel
he's still with me.

00:17:12.665 --> 00:17:14.576
I sure am, Brother Fry.

00:17:15.459 --> 00:17:18.917
Yo, big bonnet, move your ugly
but modest head covering.

00:17:19.005 --> 00:17:20.370
Ah, right,
you can't hear me.

00:17:20.506 --> 00:17:23.339
Oh, I hear you
loud and clear.

00:17:24.552 --> 00:17:26.588
You're
not Granny Hester.

00:17:26.679 --> 00:17:28.419
What have you done
with Granny Hester?

00:17:28.514 --> 00:17:30.425
She's naked
but unharmed.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:34.263
And now, Bender, it's time to
fulfill your end of the deal.

00:17:34.562 --> 00:17:36.678
Sorry, I'm not going
to kill Fry.

00:17:36.772 --> 00:17:38.603
Take me to hell
for all eternity,

00:17:38.899 --> 00:17:42.062
just as long as my little
bearded meat bag gets to live.

00:17:42.361 --> 00:17:47.105
That he will not, for you see,
it is your fate to kill him.

00:17:49.368 --> 00:17:53.987
Says you. I would never kill
Fry, not even to save my own life.

00:17:54.206 --> 00:17:56.618
But, Bender,
isn't a robot life worth

00:17:56.751 --> 00:17:59.163
ever so much more
than a human life?

00:17:59.378 --> 00:18:01.790
Of course not.
What idiot thinks that?

00:18:02.048 --> 00:18:03.458
You.

00:18:03.591 --> 00:18:07.175
You're using my own words
against me. Go to hell!

00:18:08.387 --> 00:18:10.969
Soon enough, but first, the killing.

00:18:11.057 --> 00:18:15.141
Have you noticed that animals are
sometimes spooked by robot ghosts?

00:18:15.311 --> 00:18:16.972
So what? I hate animals.

00:18:24.236 --> 00:18:26.978
Run for your life, Fry!
Move your ham flaps!

00:18:27.239 --> 00:18:28.820
He can't hear you, Bender.

00:18:28.908 --> 00:18:32.571
I'm afraid your friend is
about to be fully buckminstered!

00:18:32.703 --> 00:18:34.568
Oh, yeah? I'll just jump into a machine

00:18:34.747 --> 00:18:36.658
and get his attention
that way.

00:18:36.749 --> 00:18:39.866
Ah! But there aren't
any machines on this planet.

00:18:40.127 --> 00:18:42.413
There's one,
you rusty old dummy.

00:18:44.298 --> 00:18:46.414
Hey, no fair. Ocupado.

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:47.505
Got you.

00:18:47.593 --> 00:18:48.628
Ow! Ow!

00:18:48.719 --> 00:18:50.584
Come here, Devil.
What are you doing?

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:53.171
And Scruffy's buffet,
how's that going?

00:18:53.265 --> 00:18:56.132
Fry, Fry, look out
for that bowling barn.

00:18:58.354 --> 00:19:00.470
Bender, is that thou?

00:19:00.815 --> 00:19:04.307
I love you.

00:19:07.947 --> 00:19:09.357
Oh, my God.

00:19:09.448 --> 00:19:11.279
Did you see that?
Are you okay?

00:19:11.367 --> 00:19:12.356
What just happened?

00:19:12.535 --> 00:19:17.325
Uh. Well, I think the Robot Devil
said he loved me in Bender's voice

00:19:17.415 --> 00:19:19.406
wearing Granny Hester's
clothes.

00:19:20.042 --> 00:19:21.782
I want to go home.

00:19:23.462 --> 00:19:25.578
You still lose, Bender.

00:19:25.673 --> 00:19:29.461
You failed to kill Fry,
so you're banished to hell.

00:19:30.845 --> 00:19:32.710
I get a new body,
and you get to be

00:19:32.805 --> 00:19:35.467
a translucent chump
till the end of time.

00:19:35.766 --> 00:19:39.884
Big deal. I saved my friend.
As far as I'm concerned, I won.

00:19:39.979 --> 00:19:41.014
Oh, really?

00:19:41.981 --> 00:19:46.441
You may find your victory Pyrrhic
when subjected to this lyric

00:19:46.527 --> 00:19:49.735
For a trillion years or so

00:19:49.822 --> 00:19:50.937
Yeah.

00:19:51.615 --> 00:19:52.775
Hey, where are you going?

00:19:52.950 --> 00:19:54.656
I don't know and I don't care.

00:19:56.328 --> 00:19:59.161
Yay, I'm back.
Wait, this is my stop.

00:20:06.464 --> 00:20:07.670
Oh. This guy.

00:20:07.757 --> 00:20:11.375
Bender, for your selfless act
in saving Fry,

00:20:11.469 --> 00:20:14.586
I am pleased to welcome you
to Robot Heaven.

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:16.591
Shut up, God!
Beg pardon?

00:20:16.682 --> 00:20:19.424
I want to go back to Robot
Earth. I mean regular Earth.

00:20:22.146 --> 00:20:24.979
Hey, stop that.
I command you, you jerk.

00:20:25.691 --> 00:20:26.931
Just get out.

00:20:27.318 --> 00:20:28.524
Whoa!

00:20:32.448 --> 00:20:35.736
Whoo. I've been through
the adventure of a lifetime.

00:20:36.202 --> 00:20:37.191
Ow!

00:20:46.462 --> 00:20:47.542
I'm back, baby.

00:20:48.964 --> 00:20:50.500
You're back
from the dead?

00:20:50.591 --> 00:20:52.331
I'm back from
lots of stuff.

00:20:52.551 --> 00:20:56.043
Oh, Bender, Bender,
I missed you so much.

00:20:57.348 --> 00:20:59.304
Hey, wait, did you haunt me?